    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Reply to Bildad"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Job answered:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Yes, I know what you’ve said is true,",
          "but how can a person be justified before God?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If one wanted to take him to court,",
          "he could not answer God once in a thousand times."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God is wise and all-powerful.",
          "Who has opposed him and come out unharmed?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He removes mountains without their knowledge,",
          "overturning them in his anger."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He shakes the earth from its place",
          "so that its pillars tremble."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He commands the sun not to shine",
          "and seals off the stars."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He alone stretches out the heavens",
          "and treads on the waves of the sea."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He makes the stars: the Bear, Orion,",
          "the Pleiades, and the constellations of the southern sky."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He does great and unsearchable things,",
          "wonders without number."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If he passed by me, I wouldn’t see him;",
          "if he went by, I wouldn’t recognize him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If he snatches something, who can stop him?",
          "Who can ask him, “What are you doing? ”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God does not hold back his anger;",
          "Rahab’s assistants cringe in fear beneath him!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How then can I answer him",
          "or choose my arguments against him?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even if I were in the right, I could not answer.",
          "I could only beg my Judge for mercy."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If I summoned him and he answered me,",
          "I do not believe he would pay attention to what I said."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He batters me with a whirlwind",
          "and multiplies my wounds without cause."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He doesn’t let me catch my breath",
          "but fills me with bitter experiences."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If it is a matter of strength, look, he is the powerful one!",
          "If it is a matter of justice, who can summon him?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even if I were in the right, my own mouth would condemn me;",
          "if I were blameless, my mouth would declare me guilty."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though I am blameless,",
          "I no longer care about myself;",
          "I renounce my life."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It is all the same. Therefore I say,",
          "“He destroys both the blameless and the wicked.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When catastrophe brings sudden death,",
          "he mocks the despair of the innocent."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The earth is handed over to the wicked;",
          "he blindfolds its judges.",
          "If it isn’t he, then who is it?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My days fly by faster than a runner; ,",
          "they flee without seeing any good."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They sweep by like boats made of papyrus,",
          "like an eagle swooping down on its prey."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If I said, “I will forget my complaint,",
          "change my expression, and smile,”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I would still live in terror of all my pains.",
          "I know you will not acquit me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Since I will be found guilty,",
          "why should I struggle in vain?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If I wash myself with snow,",
          "and cleanse my hands with lye,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "then you dip me in a pit of mud,",
          "and my own clothes despise me!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For he is not a man like me, that I can answer him,",
          "that we can take each other to court."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There is no mediator between us,",
          "to lay his hand on both of us."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let him take his rod away from me",
          "so his terror will no longer frighten me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then I would speak and not fear him.",
          "But that is not the case; I am on my own."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
